## 2. Conventions

| Aspect        | Convention                                                                                                                                                                                            |
| ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Engine        | PostgreSQL 15+                                                                                                                                                                                        |
| Access        | Prisma (parameterized). Raw SQL only via tagged `$queryRaw`.                                                                                                                                          |
| Primary keys  | **Opaque prefixed text IDs** — `usr_`, `wrk_`, `src_`, `dec_`, `rev_`, `skl_`, `key_`, `inv_`, `cnv_`, `msg_`, `bld_`, `act_`. Generated by the app (`shared/helpers/ids.ts`, ULID body), not the DB. |
| Foreign keys  | Always declared; `ON DELETE` chosen per relationship (see each table).                                                                                                                                |
| Tenant column | `workspace_id` on every tenant-scoped table, first column after `id`, **NOT NULL**, FK to `workspaces`.                                                                                               |
| Column case   | `snake_case` in Postgres; mapped to `camelCase` in Prisma via `@map`.                                                                                                                                 |
| Timestamps    | `created_at` / `updated_at` `TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()`; `updated_at` maintained by the app/Prisma.                                                                                          |
| Soft delete   | `deleted_at TIMESTAMPTZ NULL` on tenant + knowledge tables; all reads filter `deleted_at IS NULL`.                                                                                                    |
| Enums         | Postgres `ENUM` types for closed sets that match the API doc's allowed values.                                                                                                                        |
| Money/counts  | `INTEGER`/`BIGINT`; no floats for counters.                                                                                                                                                           |
| JSON          | `JSONB` for genuinely variable structures (schemas, provenance, spark arrays).                                                                                                                        |

> **Why prefixed text IDs, not UUIDs:** the public API contract specifies readable,
> prefixed, opaque IDs. Storing them as the PK avoids a UUID↔public-id mapping layer.
> The AI service uses UUIDs internally; the backend references AI-service rows by an
> explicit `ai_*_id` column when needed (§10), so the two ID schemes never collide.

