## 4. Enums

```sql
CREATE TYPE member_role        AS ENUM ('admin', 'editor', 'viewer');
CREATE TYPE invite_status      AS ENUM ('pending', 'accepted', 'revoked', 'expired');
CREATE TYPE source_provider    AS ENUM ('slack', 'notion', 'github', 'jira', 'zendesk');
CREATE TYPE source_status      AS ENUM ('connected', 'disconnected', 'error', 'pending');
CREATE TYPE sync_status        AS ENUM ('healthy', 'pending', 'syncing', 'error');
CREATE TYPE decision_status    AS ENUM ('approved', 'active', 'review');
CREATE TYPE review_kind        AS ENUM ('policy_change', 'new_decision', 'contradiction', 'exception');
CREATE TYPE review_status      AS ENUM ('pending', 'approved', 'rejected');
CREATE TYPE skill_status       AS ENUM ('stable', 'active', 'draft', 'review');
CREATE TYPE build_status       AS ENUM ('queued', 'running', 'completed', 'failed', 'canceled');
CREATE TYPE message_role       AS ENUM ('user', 'assistant');
CREATE TYPE workspace_plan     AS ENUM ('trial', 'starter', 'pro', 'enterprise');
```

> Member roles follow the API doc (`admin, editor, viewer`). The AI schema's extra
> `owner` role is intentionally **not** mirrored — the backend treats the workspace
> creator as an `admin` and tracks ownership via `workspaces.created_by`.

