## 5. Identity & Tenancy

### `users` (global)

```sql
CREATE TABLE users (
  id            TEXT PRIMARY KEY,                 -- usr_…
  email         CITEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,           -- case-insensitive; CREATE EXTENSION citext
  name          TEXT,
  title         TEXT,
  avatar_color  TEXT,
  last_login_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
  created_at    TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
  updated_at    TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);
```

Auth is passwordless today (email-only signup/signin), so there is no password
column. If passwords are added, store `password_hash TEXT` (argon2id) — never
plaintext.

### `workspaces` (global tenant root)

```sql
CREATE TABLE workspaces (
  id           TEXT PRIMARY KEY,                  -- wrk_…
  name         TEXT NOT NULL,
  slug         CITEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,            -- used in {slug}.hephaestou.com/mcp
  domain       TEXT,
  plan         workspace_plan NOT NULL DEFAULT 'trial',
  seat_limit   INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 5,
  team_size    TEXT,                              -- '1-10' | '11-50' | '51-200' | '200+'
  primary_use_case TEXT,                          -- 'support' | 'ops' | 'eng' | 'agents'
  onboarding_step  TEXT,                          -- onboarding progress marker
  created_by   TEXT REFERENCES users(id),
  deleted_at   TIMESTAMPTZ,                       -- soft delete; never cascade a tenant on a misclick
  created_at   TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
  updated_at   TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);
```

`memberCount` and `usedSeats` (API doc) are derived via a count over
`workspace_members`, not stored.

### `workspace_members` (tenant-scoped, RBAC)

```sql
CREATE TABLE workspace_members (
  id           TEXT PRIMARY KEY,                  -- mem_…
  workspace_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES workspaces(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  user_id      TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  role         member_role NOT NULL DEFAULT 'viewer',
  is_active    BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE,
  invited_by   TEXT REFERENCES users(id),
  joined_at    TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
  UNIQUE (workspace_id, user_id)
);
CREATE INDEX ON workspace_members (workspace_id, user_id);
CREATE INDEX ON workspace_members (user_id);
```

This join table is the heart of multi-tenancy: it answers "which workspaces can this
user access, and as what role" and drives the `current_member_role()` RLS function.

### `invitations` (tenant-scoped)

```sql
CREATE TABLE invitations (
  id           TEXT PRIMARY KEY,                  -- inv_…
  workspace_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES workspaces(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  email        CITEXT NOT NULL,
  role         member_role NOT NULL DEFAULT 'viewer',
  token_hash   BYTEA NOT NULL UNIQUE,             -- sha256(raw token); raw token only emailed, never stored
  status       invite_status NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending',
  invited_by   TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),
  expires_at   TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now() + INTERVAL '7 days',
  accepted_at  TIMESTAMPTZ,
  created_at   TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);
CREATE INDEX ON invitations (workspace_id, email);
```

The raw invite token is a usable credential. The acceptance flow looks the user up by
`token_hash` through a privileged path (not via the tenant RLS context, since the
invitee may not yet be a member) — see §8.

