## 6. Sessions & OAuth State (global)

### `refresh_tokens`

```sql
CREATE TABLE refresh_tokens (
  id           TEXT PRIMARY KEY,                  -- rt_…
  user_id      TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  token_hash   BYTEA NOT NULL UNIQUE,             -- sha256 of the refresh token
  family_id    TEXT NOT NULL,                     -- rotation family; reuse-detection revokes the family
  expires_at   TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
  revoked_at   TIMESTAMPTZ,
  replaced_by  TEXT REFERENCES refresh_tokens(id),
  user_agent   TEXT,
  ip_address   INET,
  created_at   TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);
CREATE INDEX ON refresh_tokens (user_id);
```

Refresh tokens are **rotated on every use**: issue a new row, set `replaced_by`, and
revoke the old one. If a revoked token is presented again (reuse), revoke the whole
`family_id` — that's a theft signal.

### `oauth_states`

```sql
CREATE TABLE oauth_states (
  id            TEXT PRIMARY KEY,                 -- st_…
  user_id       TEXT REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  workspace_id  TEXT REFERENCES workspaces(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  provider      TEXT NOT NULL,
  redirect_uri  TEXT NOT NULL,
  state_hash    BYTEA NOT NULL UNIQUE,            -- signed/hashed state value
  expires_at    TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
  consumed_at   TIMESTAMPTZ,
  created_at    TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);
```

The callback validates signature, expiry, ownership, provider, and redirect URI, then
marks the row `consumed_at` (single use).

