## 9. Data Protection (No Leakage)

| Data                           | Protection                                                                                                                                          |
| ------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Provider access/refresh tokens | Encrypted at rest (`*_enc BYTEA`), via `pgcrypto` or app-layer AES-GCM with `ENCRYPTION_KEY`. Decrypted only in the integration layer at call time. |
| Webhook signing secrets        | Encrypted at rest (`secret_enc`); used only to verify inbound signatures.                                                                           |
| Workspace API keys             | Stored as `sha256` hash + short prefix. Raw key shown **once** at creation.                                                                         |
| Refresh / invite tokens        | Stored as `sha256` hash only; raw value lives only in the cookie / email.                                                                           |
| Passwords (if added)           | `argon2id` hash; never plaintext.                                                                                                                   |
| PII (emails, names)            | Returned only to authorized members of the same workspace; never logged in full.                                                                    |
| Secrets in transit             | `DATABASE_URL` uses TLS; never expose secret columns through any API field or `SELECT *` to the client.                                             |

Rules:

- Repositories **select explicit columns** for client-facing reads — never `SELECT *`
  — so encrypted/secret columns can't accidentally serialize into a response.
- The API never returns `*_enc`, `*_hash`, `key_hash`, or `token_hash` fields.
- Logs redact tokens/keys/secrets (best-practices doc §11).

